  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 results (config_024: 0.6287, config_022: 0.6186, config_013: 0.5988) consistently show that avgpool aggregation + concat fusion is the strongest combination, and pca_n2000 with imagenet_vit_l is the best RNA+image pairing tested. However, scvi_n200 (a learned RNA encoder) has never been tested in this optimal aggregation/fusion/image setting. This experiment (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) directly tests whether a learned encoder can match or exceed PCA in the best-known structural configuration. It is the highest-value next test because: (1) it isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding all other factors at their empirically best values, (2) if scvi_n200 performs comparably or better, it opens a new exploitation direction for the remaining 4 experiments, and (3) if it underperforms, it confirms PCA is the ceiling for RNA encoding and lets us focus remaining budget on fine-tuning other aspects. This is a clean, high-information experiment that reduces uncertainty about the most impactful untested design choice."
}

